# Code owners are requested for review automatically on any pull request
# touching the paths they match. Later rules win, so the specific entries
# below override the catch-all.
#
# With a single maintainer this looks redundant, and today it is. It earns its
# place at the first outside contribution and at the first Dependabot PR
# against a path where an unreviewed bump would be expensive -- the chart, the
# workflows, and the auth package are the three where a bad merge is not
# obvious from a green build.

* @NarayanaSabari

# CI and release automation. A change here can publish artifacts, grant
# permissions, or run third-party code with a repository token.
/.github/ @NarayanaSabari

# Authentication and API keys. Several past bugs in this package were things a
# passing test suite did not notice: auth silently disabled, keys in URLs, a
# route pattern that unauthenticated everything outside /v1/.
/internal/auth/ @NarayanaSabari

# Deployment surface. The chart's defaults are what an unchanged install runs.
/charts/ @NarayanaSabari
/docker/ @NarayanaSabari
/Dockerfile @NarayanaSabari
/docker-compose.yaml @NarayanaSabari

# Operational scripts: backup, restore, and the rename migration all touch
# live data.
/scripts/ @NarayanaSabari

# Public interfaces. Breaking either is a breaking change for users.
/api/proto/ @NarayanaSabari
/sdk/ @NarayanaSabari
